BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 792.00 Td (#!/bin/bash) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 780.00 Td (set -uo pipefail) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 768.00 Td (# ... [Standard path configuration] ...) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 756.00 Td (# NEW SECURITY APPROACH: Ephemeral RAM injection via --pass-fd) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 744.00 Td (# The passphrase travels through an anonymous pipe, never touching environment or argv.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 732.00 Td (CREDENTIAL_NAME="baresnap-repo-key") Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 720.00 Td (if systemd-creds list | grep -q "$CREDENTIAL_NAME"; then) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 708.00 Td (    PASS="$\(systemd-creds cat "$CREDENTIAL_NAME"\)") Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 696.00 Td (    "$BARESNAP" --pass-fd 3 create "$REPO" "$SOURCE" \\) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 684.00 Td (        >> "$LOG_FILE" 2>&1 3<<<"$PASS") Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 672.00 Td (    unset PASS) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 660.00 Td (else) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 648.00 Td (    echo "CRITICAL ERROR: Security credential not found." >&2) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 636.00 Td (    exit 2) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 624.00 Td (fi) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 600.00 Td (Explanation: --pass-fd prevents the passphrase from appearing in argv/cmdline) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 588.00 Td (The fd is closed after reading and the buffer is cleared in cleanup) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 564.00 Td (Administrator Note: To configure this on the server once,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 552.00 Td (execute:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 528.00 Td (    systemd-creds encrypt --name=baresnap-repo-key /dev/stdin -) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 504.00 Td (    \(You type the key and press Ctrl+D. The encrypted result is saved in Linux's) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 492.00 Td (    confidential credential system, bound to server hardware or systemd master keys\)) Tj ET
