BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 504.00 Td (============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 480.00 Td (NO. There is no automatic command \(like 'convert' or 'migrate'\) to) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 468.00 Td (recompress the history of a repository. The initial configuration is) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 456.00 Td (hardcoded into the central 'config' file and old blocks are) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 444.00 Td (immutable.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 420.00 Td (Starting from version v2.3.0, what you can do is change the compression) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 408.00 Td (strategy for NEW backups of that same repository using) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 396.00 Td (command-line session variables \(e.g., forcing ZSTD over an LZ4 repo\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 372.00 Td (New data will use the new algorithm and old ones will remain as) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 360.00 Td (they were, coexisting in the same pool.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 336.00 Td (If what you need is to change the algorithm UNIFORMLY for the entire) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 324.00 Td (repository \(including past backups\), the manual procedure) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 312.00 Td (remains the only path:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 288.00 Td (1. Create a new repo with desired compression in init.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 276.00 Td (2. Restore the snapshot of the old repo to disk \(full restore\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 264.00 Td (3. Do 'create' from disk to new repo.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 252.00 Td (4. Verify structural consistency with "baresnap verify".) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 240.00 Td (5. Delete the old repo.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 216.00 Td (============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 204.00 Td (22.6 WHAT HAPPENS IF THERE IS A POWER OUTAGE DURING A BACKUP?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 192.00 Td (============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 168.00 Td (The repo is NEVER left in an unrepairable state. Guaranteed by design:) Tj ET
