BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 408.00 Td (============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 384.00 Td (NO. BareSnap uses Linux-specific POSIX calls and is designed) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 372.00 Td (exclusively for x86_64 and ARM64 \(aarch64\) architectures on Linux.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 348.00 Td (The strict use of calls like getrandom, utimensat, and /dev/tty rules out) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 336.00 Td (macOS and Windows. This limits its viability as a universal corporate) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 324.00 Td (tool for mixed fleets, but guarantees performance and) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 312.00 Td (spartan simplicity in pure Linux environments \(from a 2007 Core 2 Duo) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 300.00 Td (up to a modern Raspberry Pi 5\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 276.00 Td (For Windows, use Restic. For Mac, use Restic or Borg.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 252.00 Td (============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 240.00 Td (22.9 WHAT IF I FORGET THE PASSPHRASE?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 228.00 Td (============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 204.00 Td (Data is UNRECOVERABLE. There is no backdoor, no recovery key,) Tj ET
