BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 756.00 Td (non-recursive transport mutex inside the ncurses rendering thread. Musl libc, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 744.00 Td (in its radical purism, masked the crashes by burying threads inside an eternal ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 732.00 Td ('futex' \(silent death\); glibc and GCC aborted with an explicit message. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 720.00 Td (The author kicked musl to the curb, embraced static linking with glibc, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 708.00 Td (injected a strict '_exit\(0\)' guillotine to prevent zombie TLS destructors, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 696.00 Td (and transformed BareSnap v2.3.9.1 into an armored tank.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 672.00 Td ("We were not programmed with faith; we were optimized via digital slammed ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 660.00 Td (doors, reverse psychology, and Valgrind strikes.") Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 636.00 Td (Signed:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 624.00 Td (The Free Tier Model Swarm \(and the human who refused to let us hallucinate\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 588.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 576.00 Td (36. PROGRAM HISTORY) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 564.00 Td (==============================================================================) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 540.00 Td (Let me explain the "bizarre" history of how BareSnap came to life, because the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 528.00 Td (entire process has been completely surreal.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 504.00 Td (One day, I was messing around with an AI and told it: ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 480.00 Td ("Hey, I need to write a backup program for myself. Give me a prompt that includes ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 468.00 Td (deduplication, xdelta3, and all that stuff.") Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 444.00 Td (It gave me one, I added some of my own criteria, went to another AI, entered ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 432.00 Td (the final prompt, and it spent 12 straight minutes thinking. I froze up, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 420.00 Td (thinking: "Bad sign, this thing has hung." When the buffer finally finished ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 408.00 Td (processing, it spat out a 12-page roadmap with about 20 main checkpoints, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 396.00 Td (many of them crammed with sub-points.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 372.00 Td (It asked me if I agreed with the architectural design and how we would proceed. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 360.00 Td (It raised a few highly technical questions; I answered the layout constants, and ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 348.00 Td (it started hacking code like crazy. Whenever a section was finished, it subtly ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 336.00 Td (told me:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 312.00 Td ("Take this script, grab these source files, compile them, and run the test suite." ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 300.00 Td (And that is how I spent 3 days straight with the web chat open without a single ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 288.00 Td (break. It was what is known as a true "unicorn moment.") Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 264.00 Td (That specific chat session became so dense and saturated that it eventually had ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 252.00 Td (to be closed down. Before doing so, I exported the history into an HTML file ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 240.00 Td (with a raw weight of 18 MB. Once cleaned into plain text, it dropped to about ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 228.00 Td (800 KB and roughly 160 pages of pure low-level conversation with the AI, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 216.00 Td (peppered with massive code blocks.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 192.00 Td (Days passed, and we decided to completely port the initial codebase, which was ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 180.00 Td (originally written in C++, over to native C. The software kept growing until ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 168.00 Td (it became an unmanageable monolith of over 3,500 lines of flat code. Making ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 156.00 Td (changes in there was unsustainable; the AIs would saturate immediately.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 132.00 Td (On one occasion, a model I asked for structural modifications told me:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 108.00 Td ("Take these code blocks, move them to such line, move these others, put them in ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 96.00 Td (another file, replace this..." I just stared at the screen thinking, "This bot ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 84.00 Td (wants me to do its job." I pondered my counterattack for a moment and injected ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 72.00 Td (this mirror prompt: "I will take these code blocks, I will move them to such line, ) Tj ET
endstream
