BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 792.00 Td (I will move these others, I will put them in another file, I will replace this...", ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 780.00 Td (stripped the quotation marks, and added at the bottom: "Excellent, whenever you ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 768.00 Td (are ready." I hit enter, and the bot started making all the modifications by itself. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 756.00 Td (I had to use that exact same psychological strategy with that AI twice in a row.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 732.00 Td (At one point, a graphical user interface \(GUI\) using Dear ImGui was implemented. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 720.00 Td (Even though it worked perfectly, it just didn't convince me for the purpose of ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 708.00 Td (this project.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 684.00 Td (The C++ era was behind us; the monolith in front of me was now written in C, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 672.00 Td (but it was still a giant block of code. So I told myself: ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 660.00 Td ("This has to be refactored...". I started analyzing my options: "Since i am refactoring ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 648.00 Td (anyway, I might as well split it into independent modules." One day, I took the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 636.00 Td (monolithic code, went to an AI, and asked: "Hey, give me a hand with this refactoring.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 624.00 Td (" It sat there thinking for about 5 minutes and returned a Bash script with an embedded ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 612.00 Td (Python block. I ran it in the terminal, and the refactoring took literally less than a ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 600.00 Td (second: it split the monolith into 1 internal header and 7 .c modules, keeping the public ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 588.00 Td (API completely intact and memory offsets perfectly clean.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 564.00 Td (The following days flew by in non-stop development marathons: 100 tests, xdelta3, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 552.00 Td (xchacha, zstd, 200 tests, 450, 800, crashes, segmentation faults, bugs, intense ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 540.00 Td (debugging sessions, algorithmic lies, code betrayals, strace, AddressSanitizer \(ASan\), ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 528.00 Td (tsan, and Valgrind. I subjected the program to the entire integrated test suite. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 516.00 Td (We also implemented the VFS layer over SSH, since the software was originally ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 504.00 Td (conceived solely for local use.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 480.00 Td (There was a watershed moment during development when we discovered that SSH backups ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 468.00 Td (were severely bottlenecked at around 800 MB; if the payload exceeded that size, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 456.00 Td (the data arrived corrupted at the remote destination. We found this out when trying ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 444.00 Td (to run a real-world backup of the Linux Mint ISO library \(around 8.1 GB\). ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 432.00 Td (Handling that volume of data on legacy hardware \(a 2007 Intel Core 2 Duo CPU with ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 420.00 Td (4 GB of RAM\) while managing LZ4 compression and the deduplication tree is a complex, g) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 408.00 Td (rueling process for old silicon.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 384.00 Td (Near the end of the marathon, I ended up working with an AI model that only ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 372.00 Td (accepted plain text via web chat \(no file uploads or attachments allowed\). ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 360.00 Td (I looked at the machine's system clock and thought: "Tonight is going to be a ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 348.00 Td (long night." After nearly 6 consecutive hours of non-stop iterations, we finally ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 336.00 Td (fixed the VFS network bug. A grueling 'verify' command \(requiring 20 full wall-clock ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 324.00 Td (minutes to recalculate hashes\) confirmed absolute integrity. I extracted test data, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 312.00 Td (and everything worked flawlessly.) Tj ET
