BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 756.00 Td (That was the crucial breakthrough \(one of many in the trenches\). ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 744.00 Td (When closing the session, the AI itself dropped a line that has remained ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 732.00 Td (permanently etched into the architecture: ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 708.00 Td ("It has been a slaughterhouse of iterations, but it closed with data, not with faith.") Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 684.00 Td (Deeply pragmatic design decisions had to be made along the way, such as:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 660.00 Td (- Discarding the graphical GUI to focus 100% on the TUI \(Terminal User Interface\); ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 648.00 Td (the GUI based on 'yad' just wasn’t up to the task, as previously noted.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 624.00 Td (- Balancing network RPCs: they could be reduced in quantity, but then the overall ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 612.00 Td (execution time ballooned and more junk data than necessary was downloaded.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 588.00 Td (- Eliminating Xdelta3 calculations during SSH transfers to drastically boost) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 576.00 Td ( network speed in exchange for a controlled increase in physical storage footprint.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 552.00 Td (- And countles other low-level optimizations that I can no longer even remember.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 528.00 Td (There have been good weeks, bad weeks, and average weeks; brutal marathons, burnouts, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 516.00 Td (and roadblocks. Days have passed, and the total iterations now count in the hundreds ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 504.00 Td (\(maybe thousands?\). I wouldn’t recommend anyone to develop this way unless ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 492.00 Td (they possess infinite patience; if you are the type to get frustrated or angry after) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 480.00 Td ( spending 4 hours fighting different prompts across multiple web chats using free-tier ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 468.00 Td (models, this methodology is not for you.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 444.00 Td (It is common to see the exact same AI completely contradict itself after a single ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 432.00 Td (iteration and tell you in surprise: "Look! That other AI left a trap for you in the code! ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 420.00 Td (That’s why it wasn’t working, let’s fix it." And the funny thing is that sometimes ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 408.00 Td (it actually fixes it; other times it makes it worse, and sometimes it just gives ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 396.00 Td (up and tells you: "Let’s leave it at that, let’s talk about something else.") Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 372.00 Td (Now, with this new final version \(v2.4.0\), I look back and realize everything ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 360.00 Td (started just 40 days ago. Today we have our own lore, debugging logs worthy of ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 348.00 Td (Sherlock Holmes, a massive manual spanning over 169 pages, and a backup utility ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 336.00 Td (featuring double encryption, double compression, local xdelta3, integrated VFS ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 324.00 Td (over SSH, a TUI interface, and a battery of nearly 1,000 tests—amounting to 18,279 ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 312.00 Td (lines of pure C across 761,838 bytes of source code.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 288.00 Td (I don’t know if people will actually end up using this program, if they will tear ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 276.00 Td (it apart out of pure curiosity, or if it will simply be ignored within the immense ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 264.00 Td (noise of the internet. But one thing is for sure: attempting to forge an infrastructure ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 252.00 Td (of this caliber using nothing but web-chat prompts on a Free Tier plan is a feat i ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 240.00 Td (wouldn’t recommend to just anyone.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 216.00 Td (Oh, and I highly recommend reading "The Mysteries of Sherlock Holmes" located ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 50.00 204.00 Td (in the assets directory.) Tj ET
